s rumors abound of possible heirs born out of wedlock.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit leaders urge 'maximum restraint' in Middle East</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63fbdd7e4840778d6a66b01901c07ae2db0fa41232469b61cca654063387dd91</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239--4541a165cd4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The joint delcaration at the BRICS 2026 summit expressed 'deep concern' over escalation of tensions in the Middle East. China's President Xi.Jingping said the Iran war was not in the bloc's interest. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian GRU spies behind failed Leipzig attack: reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e35bfec078c46ec24669e15247c5853e77fbe4e5bf0e50a4461ef9c6eca18b5d</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858--97143d694fa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German newspaper has cited reports tying a failed attack at Leipzig Airport to Moscow's GRU military intelligence agency. One suspect's ties to GRU were known when he entered the country, yet he was not surveilled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Flavio Bolsonaro faces corruption probe weeks before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb95c75de9a687e00f00743f0ab12cd2ef8fff8ef67b529ea38791901fd1a783</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-faces-corruption-probe-weeks-before-election/a-79242561--f6206eb40070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-faces-corruption-probe-weeks-before-election/a-79242561?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazilian Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, Lula's top rival in next month's election, is under investigation for alleged corruption linked to financing a biopic about his father, former President Jair Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Corals as climate archive: Are El Ninos intensifying?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2a33157da21fc07e58ad5f394e38d9a2b412d3d5c012b8121320acac9792931</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-ninos-intensifying/a-79243425--052f407fd862.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-ninos-intensifying/a-79243425?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Records from the past few decades show that, during this period, El Nino events have been frequent and often extreme. But is this normal, or is it the result of climate change? Corals can give us a clear indication.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uber leaves two key African markets — and their drivers in despair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a779aaec64101c867241d1c98fd38e3e5279974ab83ade98fab3c153410006a</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189--bdbc88dc3498.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uber's departure from Nigeria and Uganda has left countless customers high and dry. But what about drivers? With fuel prices, maintenance, and other operating costs rising, many say they're struggling to make a living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires multiple ballistic missiles day after trilateral drills end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2efc866caf1436fb962b8c27fa696526f84c0a9e2baea55d5d48a6bc3d2dc22f</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-fires-multiple-ballistic-missiles-day-after-trilateral-drills-end/a-79242070--1cf7a7ff23e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-fires-multiple-ballistic-missiles-day-after-trilateral-drills-end/a-79242070?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea launched several short-range ballistic missiles into the sea a day after the US, South Korea and Japan concluded joint military exercises Pyongyang had called provocative.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's drone war comes to Moldova and Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5192c7dfd9b07cf218d5e400f90da31e2573678b6b63d2c1a4906480a5a29728</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591--15076a5f335b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Incursions by Russian drones into Moldovan and Romanian airspace are increasingly common. This week the Ukrainian president's plane was stopped from taking off from Chisinau. Observers suspect the attacks are deliberate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>DW exclusive: Zelenskyy offers to meet Putin at G20 in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17982e34ea11ab0d87d73f670c1bd8aec65a691ca6a5b7ec88b37313ddeb7d29</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703--3aacfd955f7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an interview with DW, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said his country was in a strong position to negotiate and offered to meet Vladimir Putin in Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Sabotage suspected in train derailment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a1ba1bf4b6033abf99eb48e2455c8ca5d3151c012f6ce6c76b560ef34b9a08e</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T21:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-sabotage-suspected-in-train-derailment/a-79241365--a85bafd6493b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-sabotage-suspected-in-train-derailment/a-79241365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens were injured when a train derailed between Rouen and Caen in Normandy, northwest France, on Friday evening. Police believe the accident may have been deliberately caused, local media say.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russian strike on Kyiv gas station kills 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:090ccb533a3ebb79e9e21db52303e8000e0033e83b837948a65d21822968412b</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russian-strike-on-kyiv-gas-station-kills-2/a-79238219--1e875d361611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russian-strike-on-kyiv-gas-station-kills-2/a-79238219?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With fighting on the front lines mostly stalled, Russia has been increasingly hitting petrol stations and other civilian targets. Ukraine has also been attacking Russia with drones, killing three people on Friday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US commemorates 25 years since 9/11 terror attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16536357db94fa38c5e3a3490dd6261446562efff6166da2245b3ad9915408bd</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-commemorates-25-years-since-9-11-terror-attack/a-79237898--048849ac59b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-commemorates-25-years-since-9-11-terror-attack/a-79237898?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter century has passed since Islamists hijacked four commercial jets and turned them into weapons against the US. On Friday, ceremonies in New York, Pennsylvania and Washington DC marked the dark anniversary.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran pursues cautious escalation ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7b3f846409b6e4b5f3b5eefdfdb37a8b5b325625986d1f88f28c6fbbf150462</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061--fcf56cfd7af3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tehran appears to be boosting pressure on Washington ahead of the crucial midterm vote, but shows little desire to return to a full-scale war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's BRICS strategy tested with Xi, Putin set to visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24e4dbb8d74f9cf2528d1c86d8687d4ecca0483a6c981a10ba036ad47911f556</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879--3d59ee566cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New Delhi's "America Plus" approach sees India deepening its ties with China and Russia, while also trying to keep BRICS from turning into an anti-Western platform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war: Saudi-Houthi escalation intensifies Yemen conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6559b3b4fd41d3a23aff553acea0f60382eab022f22990d084c3a60a51c462d6</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627--c5b66c310724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthi takeovers of Mokha, Dhubab and Perim in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait threaten to push Yemen deeper into the Middle East war. The Iran-backed group has made advances against Yemen's government and Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany charges 7 suspected Hamas members over attack plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4262f2047b055ee5cfe673b8f1e4ed5538ce7880e3886a6c5c2f8f071da3b58a</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171--a30b5fe0228d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors say the suspects had moved beyond general preparations and were already pursuing a concrete plan for a deadly attack on Israeli or Jewish targets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>9/11 conspiracy theories that continue to circulate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d072368185d5db49c0231844515dd6ed43ccf0f88f0bf33bde0453ace5f6df2</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/9-11-conspiracy-theories-that-continue-to-circulate/a-78896069--975de526f230.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/9-11-conspiracy-theories-that-continue-to-circulate/a-78896069?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter-century after the September 11, 2001, attacks, they are still the focus of numerous conspiracy theories. Why do people believe them?</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:286234b624cb12fd43252b325b475cd010653ec49e719f372c57efa9dfe24018</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec549c549b3ed62527323bc71edffb1e8f0637881a8c8423e14fc370835c678</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthis tighten control of strategic Red Sea towns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35b4e3a035fe9fe5e3bdd26c1dc634657317fd5d34cc222282b9870a924f5d59</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-tighten-control-of-strategic-red-sea-towns/a-79220628--4b086e3863b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-tighten-control-of-strategic-red-sea-towns/a-79220628?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reports indicate Houthi militants have taken over the port city of Mokha along with Perim Island, which occupies a strategic position on a vital transport waterway in the Red Sea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
